  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 17-layer MgF2/Al2O3 defect-cavity bandpass filter on fused silica substrate. Layer sequence: L1(MgF2), L2(Al2O3), L3(MgF2), L4(Al2O3), L5(MgF2), L6(Al2O3), L7(MgF2), L8(Al2O3), L9(MgF2), L10(Al2O3-defect), L11(MgF2), L12(Al2O3), L13(MgF2), L14(Al2O3), L15(MgF2), L16(Al2O3), L17(MgF2). Impose bilateral symmetry: thickness(L13)=thickness(L16), thickness(L6)=thickness(L15), thickness(L7)=thickness(L14). Initialize thicknesses at round-2 medians: defect L10=85.5 nm, inner mirrors L1-L6=44.0 nm, outer mirrors L11-L16=47.0 nm. Apply ±5 nm bounds around these medians. Use L-BFGS-B optimizer with max function evaluations=500, tolerance=1e-5. Spectral targets: maximize transmittance 255–280 nm, minimize transmittance 300–700 nm and 700–1100 nm. Air incidence, unpolarized. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 255-280 nm, 300-700 nm, 700-1100 nm. soft objectives: high transmittance in 255–280 nm; low transmittance in 300–700 nm; low transmittance in 700–1100 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: transmittance in 300–700 nm; transmittance in 700–1100 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layers ≤ 30; no metal layers; conventional depositable inorganic dielectric materials only.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Optimize a 17-layer symmetric bandpass filter on fused silica using alternating MgF2 and Al2O3 layers, starting from given median thicknesses with ±5 nm bounds, to maximize transmittance in the 255–280 nm band while minimizing transmittance across 300–700 nm and 700–1100 nm under normal unpolarized illumination.",
